            {
                "entry_id": "4488ac85-3f8c-38fc-9e0b-01aa6eb63898",
                "word": "roucoulade",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e95fd30d-f1b0-49ef-89df-d9d5a940b7d8",
                        "entry_id": "4488ac85-3f8c-38fc-9e0b-01aa6eb63898",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "roucoulades"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "54c5aea7-8132-33cc-a2e6-2bab279926b1",
                        "entry_id": "4488ac85-3f8c-38fc-9e0b-01aa6eb63898",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Bruit que font les pigeons et les tourterelles en roucoulant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d04235c-22f1-4f04-ba60-c9be2c91985a",
                                "sense_id": "54c5aea7-8132-33cc-a2e6-2bab279926b1",
                                "text": "Un pigeon ne passe pas inaperçu … ; mais je ne perçois pas plus de roucoulades que de symphonie de Beethoven dans les couloirs du métro. En fait de volaille, je ne perçois qu’un rossignol qui s’égosille sous les frais ombrages..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab21b73b-542b-4242-af4d-22f72dd1e6c7",
                                "sense_id": "54c5aea7-8132-33cc-a2e6-2bab279926b1",
                                "text": "Il nous fait signe de rester immobiles, arrondit les lèvres, puis imite la roucoulade d’un oiseau chanteur."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "53fc71a8-f8ad-3c98-b5bd-c406967e3f64",
                        "entry_id": "4488ac85-3f8c-38fc-9e0b-01aa6eb63898",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Parole douce, souvent répétitive ou peu nuancée."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "24793f3a-028d-44d6-bbcc-e9088d74ea9b",
                                "sense_id": "53fc71a8-f8ad-3c98-b5bd-c406967e3f64",
                                "text": "Est-ce sa faute ou celle de l’auteur ? comment passer si vite d’une diction large et sentie à une roucoulade sans expression ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2209c9bd-f3b0-4bbe-8d2d-14c3d879a441",
                                "sense_id": "53fc71a8-f8ad-3c98-b5bd-c406967e3f64",
                                "text": "Enfin, depuis les Maures, la musique copte ou égyptienne s’est rangée au niveau de celle des races sémitiques et tatares : ce n’est plus qu’une sorte de roucoulade incertaine de motif, chargée de fioritures, sans modulation régulière, mais semée d’intonation dystoniques, qui, roulant au hasard sur une basse invariable, ressemble à part l’exagération des termes, aux divers bruits de la foudre, mêlés au sourd mugissement des vents."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68fbd03d-d9e0-4f3e-8b89-3e7c91956670",
                                "sense_id": "53fc71a8-f8ad-3c98-b5bd-c406967e3f64",
                                "text": "Vous comprenez, ma petite vieille, je vous ai fait des roucoulades comme ça, mais au fond je n’en pense pas un mot. C’était pour mon coup."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4447f5d4-d7d2-47f8-a24f-eb45d5f58464",
                                "sense_id": "53fc71a8-f8ad-3c98-b5bd-c406967e3f64",
                                "text": "En vérité, même si j’ai dit tout à l’heure que Cau et moi étions passés maîtres dans l’art de la séduction par les mots, je hais profondément, de tout mon être, les figures obligées de la roucoulade, temps perdu, paroles convenues, du vent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "84ba4a82-568f-4714-b87a-5620608f6149",
                        "source_entry_id": "4488ac85-3f8c-38fc-9e0b-01aa6eb63898",
                        "target_lang_word": "coo",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "coo",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "066170a2-23b2-3002-8cae-be9fd35afac0",
                                        "entry_id": "8e0e621b-d07d-3b23-98f8-d5ce12710c0b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The murmuring sound made by a dove or pigeon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73881e00-2079-45fc-ab20-682c22e7784f",
                                                "sense_id": "066170a2-23b2-3002-8cae-be9fd35afac0",
                                                "text": "The male [ring dove] will continue nest-coos for 3–4 days until his female partner begins to nest-coo. At that point the male's nest-coo begins to become less frequent[…]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "711a5530-d937-3d75-b6cc-8263d1b90d94",
                                        "entry_id": "8e0e621b-d07d-3b23-98f8-d5ce12710c0b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An expression of pleasure made by a person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e4b21ad-8e7b-4c53-9044-f270c4818458",
                                                "sense_id": "711a5530-d937-3d75-b6cc-8263d1b90d94",
                                                "text": "An infant has only cries and coos with which to communicate distress and well-being. Adults have many more ways of expressing themselves. However, their expressions of disease and ease can be boiled down to sophisticated cries and coos. A call for help in whatever form is a cry. A sense of well-being however expressed is a coo. Healing in the context of cries and coos can be viewed as the process of resolving the cries and fostering the coos."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "coo",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41d450a9-c2ce-3f9f-a108-b051ffc49014",
                                        "entry_id": "b3637b08-21c8-332d-afd8-802dd4b5de0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make a soft murmuring sound, as a pigeon."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99397ea7-ae3b-4d9d-bbcb-8f14850be389",
                                                "sense_id": "41d450a9-c2ce-3f9f-a108-b051ffc49014",
                                                "text": "No birds, except as birds of paſſage, flew, / No bee was known to hum, no dove to coo."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e4e0596-4a1b-4497-865b-1105ec0dc987",
                                                "sense_id": "41d450a9-c2ce-3f9f-a108-b051ffc49014",
                                                "text": "DUET—MAYOR and MAUD. […] Like a Dove I'll coo and bill, pretty Maud, / I will not coo and bill, Mr. Mayor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f165d644-b52e-4d65-85cc-560bc786c11a",
                                                "sense_id": "41d450a9-c2ce-3f9f-a108-b051ffc49014",
                                                "text": "But oh! ſhall I, Misfortune's bondman, ſpeak / Of pleaſures and delights, where ſorrows ſhriek! / Can plaintive nightingale, or turte-dove, / When vultures tear them, ſing or coo of love?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "befcdecc-718d-4c78-8951-55fec1d0fad0",
                                                "sense_id": "41d450a9-c2ce-3f9f-a108-b051ffc49014",
                                                "text": "The black-bird and the speckled thrush / Good-morrow gave from brake and brush; / In answer cooed the cushat dove, / Her notes of peace, and rest, and love."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2de5995-7a27-40dc-a4eb-229e6a70ca85",
                                                "sense_id": "41d450a9-c2ce-3f9f-a108-b051ffc49014",
                                                "text": "Then did her soft breath stop and she lay still, her eyes yet open and smiling at the blossoms and the doves who sat upon the window-ledge and lowly cooed and cooed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "085436f0-6cf4-481c-ae1e-26c4c6e79b15",
                                                "sense_id": "41d450a9-c2ce-3f9f-a108-b051ffc49014",
                                                "text": "As Norah Jones coos sweet nothings on the soundtrack, the happy couple—played by Paul Rudd and Amy Poehler—canoodle through a Manhattan montage, making pasta for two, swimming through a pile of autumn leaves, and horsing around at a fruit stand."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "70691296-d893-316d-9672-95ba98404e8e",
                                        "entry_id": "b3637b08-21c8-332d-afd8-802dd4b5de0c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To speak in an admiring fashion, to be enthusiastic about."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fe4e4ae-e816-418b-a7dd-c003a86a9439",
                                                "sense_id": "70691296-d893-316d-9672-95ba98404e8e",
                                                "text": "They were too busy cooing over the baby and his parents were too busy cooing over each other."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "coo",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b84eaa60-c0a3-34c5-a519-d40373ecf3c3",
                                        "entry_id": "50d17185-be1f-3d9f-bbe8-a97838d9c0ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cool."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "coo",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "35c3fb23-fd05-3435-9858-bb8b1ab27e7b",
                                        "entry_id": "51d09c27-a0ec-30c0-acf7-79c8d1e57503",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An expression of approval, fright, surprise, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cebd1b63-76f3-4e22-9efc-a4f3b6c4659b",
                                                "sense_id": "35c3fb23-fd05-3435-9858-bb8b1ab27e7b",
                                                "text": "I stood outside the door for a space, letting \"I dare not\" wait upon \"I would\", as Jeeves tells me cats do in adages, then turned the handle softly, pushed – also softly – and, carrying on into the interior, found myself confronted by a girl in housemaid's costume who put a hand to her throat like somebody in a play and leaped several inches in the direction of the ceiling. \"Coo!\" she said, having returned to terra firma and taken aboard a spot of breath. \"You gave me a start, sir!\" […] \"If you cast an eye on him, you will see that he's asleep now.\" \"Coo! So he is.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f46de13b-b1fe-46c1-8260-78774dd3a659",
                                                "sense_id": "35c3fb23-fd05-3435-9858-bb8b1ab27e7b",
                                                "text": "The last track on each of the three sections is a professional course, where you can customise your bike by changing the tyres and the size of chainwheel. Coo!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a02ed9f7-dc3f-4fb5-87f1-84539a7e19b6",
                                                "sense_id": "35c3fb23-fd05-3435-9858-bb8b1ab27e7b",
                                                "text": "We want you to come up with a side splitting caption for a picture drawn by the fair hand of those at System 3. If you turn out to be the Funniest \"Person\", we'll give you a big wopping model of a dinosaur. Coo."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2f40eef6-ee77-43ae-bd8c-35e3d01299ee",
                                                "sense_id": "35c3fb23-fd05-3435-9858-bb8b1ab27e7b",
                                                "text": "Coo, I've only had four gallons of extra caffeine coffee today so I'm not my usual talking-to-PR-girlies-for-hours-on-end self. But bear with me a mo while I get myself together (audience waits for an age while he searches through his coat for the golden envelope). Here it is! Coo, and the winner is The NewZealand Story."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
